--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SlowQueriesPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
SlowQueriesDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web SlowQueryRow /
SlowQueriesResponse / SlowQueryOrderBy 1:1 (production binds the KMP
OperatorConfidenceStore.slowQueries feed, GET /admin/observability/slow-queries
[order_by, limit], through the seam). The page is the operator-observability
"top-N pg_stat_statements" surface: a sortable, limit-capped table of the slowest
queries with the fingerprint, call count, mean/max/total ms timings, rows returned,
and the shared-buffer cache-hit ratio so operators can tell "slow but cached" from
"slow because of I/O".

One query drives the page, so its data states are switched in place — never a blank
region. The single web GlassPanel is reproduced:

  GlassPanel1 — the top-queries panel (web `GlassPanel` p-6): a PanelTitle plus the
    Order-by + Limit selects (web `ORDER_BY_OPTIONS` / `LIMIT_OPTIONS`), and the
    body that switches loading skeleton ⇄ big EmptyState ⇄ 503 empty-table note ⇄
    the adaptive DataTable. (SlowQueriesPage.swift > queriesPanel; the order/limit
    pickers re-query via SlowQueriesPageModel.reload, web useSlowQueries(orderBy,limit)).

The adaptive table (web `DataTable`, 7 columns) is a horizontally-aligned columnar
Grid on macOS/iPad regular width and per-query cards on compact iPhone width
(SlowQueriesPage.Table.swift > SlowQueriesTable). The pure web display logic was
ported 1:1 + unit-tested: fmtNumber (en-US grouping, fixed precision — the web
module default is 2), the total/mean/max decimal places, and cacheHitRatio
(hit/(hit+read)*100 to 1 dp, em-dash when there were no buffer accesses), plus the
fingerprint `|| '—'` fallback. The 503 SUBSYSTEM_NOT_CONFIGURED branch surfaces the
web subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner + the DataTable empty message; a generic
failure shows the PageContainer error panel + Retry.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesModels.swift            (value types/result/seam/sample/state/formatters)
  Sources/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesPageModel.swift         (@Observable model + reorder/limit re-query)
  Sources/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesPage.swift              (chrome + 4 states + GlassPanel1 + controls)
  Sources/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesPage.Table.swift        (adaptive 7-column table / cards)
  Sources/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesRouteRegistration.swift (.slowQueries route)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/SlowQueriesPageModelTests.swift (state-machine + display-logic tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift          (MOD: +.slowQueries case / pathSegment / icon / System group)
  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift    (MOD: +"/admin/slow-queries" alias)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift          (MOD: wire SlowQueriesRouteRegistration into routeHostRegistry)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings  (MOD: +21 bare keys: 16 admin.slowQueries.* + 4 order-option
                                       labels + route.slowQueries; admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle
                                       already existed and was reused)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json       (MOD: +2 rows page:admin/SlowQueries 22/22 macos+ios)

Navigation reconciliation: the web route is the admin sub-path /admin/slow-queries,
which AppRouteParser resolves to the dedicated .slowQueries route (pathSegment
"slow-queries", System sidebar group, "timer" SF Symbol) via a path alias —
mirroring the sibling .schemaDrift (/admin/schema-drift) pattern — reachable +
deep-linkable without displacing other admin pages. The generated TeslaSync.xcodeproj
+ the built Frameworks/Shared.xcframework are git-ignored.

